knotify watches files and directories and reports what changes on
standard output: by default one JSON object per event, optionally
filtered by kind (create, modify, remove, rename).

Its ETF mode (--protocol etf) is meant for Erlang and Elixir programs
that run it as a port. It sends batches of changed paths, relative to
one root and byte-exact, as length-prefixed Erlang terms, with credits
for flow control and rescan requests when events are lost. KnotifyEx is
the Elixir library that drives it.

It is built on the notify crate, which uses kqueue(2) on FreeBSD.
